  "description": "<p>Created from Slack question (<a href=\"https://fedora-project.slack.com/archives/C8B5TSR4J/p1692029486878149\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://fedora-project.slack.com/archives/C8B5TSR4J/p1692029486878149</a>):</p>\n\n<p>Fedora 6 does support the usage of hash URIs on NonRDFSources, but they are not visible on the Admin UI (section \"Other resources\" is missing for NonRDFSources on the Fedora UI).</p>\n\n<p>A put to &lt;NonRDFSource-URI&gt;/fcr:metadata that includes such HashURIs (e.g with triples like &lt;NonRDFSource-URI&gt;#&lt;someHash&gt; &lt;somePredicate&gt; \"someLIteral\") is accepted. The additional resources are returned correctly on the API.</p>",
